407 0 obj
<<
/A 1290 0 R
/Alt (Five line graphs compare drug concentration over time in healthy and type 2 diabetes subjects for MDZ, DAB, PTV, RSV, and ATV, each representing specific transporters or enzymes. Healthy subjects are shown with a pink line and type two diabetes subjects with a blue line. For panels a, b and e, type 2 diabetes often shows higher or prolonged drug concentrations than healthy subjects, with variability in each profile. Axes are labeled for concentration in picograms per milliliter and time in hours, with error bars on data points. Panel labels and transporter or enzyme associations are prominently displayed within each graph.)
/K [39 1291 0 R]
/P 114 0 R
/Pg 41 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (FIGURE 1)
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
