425 0 obj
<<
/A 1306 0 R
/Alt (Four pharmacokinetic compartment diagrams labeled a, b, c, and d are shown. Diagram a illustrates a dose entering compartment C1 with volume VC via rate Ka, distributing to peripheral compartment C2 with volume VT, and eliminated by CL/F, with Q/F indicating inter-compartmental clearance. Diagram b shows dose split into two pathways, one with first-order input \(Ka, F1\), the other with zero-order input \(D2, 1-F1\), both leading to C1 and peripheral C2, with CL/F and Q/F. Diagram c is similar to b but adds ALAG1 with first-order input, omitting the peripheral compartment. Diagram d shows a dose administered by zero-order input \(D2\) to C1, then distributed to C2 with Q/F and eliminated by CL/F.)
/K [26 1307 0 R]
/P 127 0 R
/Pg 42 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (FIGURE 2)
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
